@startuml operator-rbac-reach
' Where the operator ServiceAccount can reach, split by the same three grant families as the gateway.
' Source of truth: docs/src/security/rbac.md
!include _style.puml

skinparam wrapWidth 350
skinparam nodesep 18
skinparam ranksep 34
skinparam rectangle {
  roundCorner 4
}

rectangle "**Operator ServiceAccount**\nkaalm-system/kaalm-controller" as OPSA #back:87CEEB;line:0D47A1;line.bold;text:0a2540

' ---------- family 1: ClusterRole ----------
rectangle "**reach: every namespace in the cluster**\na ClusterRoleBinding cannot be namespace-limited" as band #line:B71C1C;line.dashed;text:B71C1C {
  rectangle "**Kaalm CRDs**\nAgent, AgentTask, AgentChannel,\nModelProvider, ToolProvider, AgentClass\n**get, list, watch, update, patch**\n(delete on AgentTask, for TTL cleanup)\n....\n***/status**  **get, update, patch**\nseparate grants: with the status\nsubresource enabled, write on the main\nresource does **not** permit status writes\n....\n***/finalizers**  **update**\nreconcilers set ownerRefs with\nblockOwnerDeletion: true, and the\nOwnerReferencesPermissionEnforcement\nadmission plugin authorizes that against\nthe owner's finalizers subresource\n....\n**customresourcedefinitions**  **get**\n**customresourcedefinitions/status**  **patch**\nresourceNames: the six Kaalm CRDs,\nfor the storage-version migrator" as crds #back:F5F5F5;line:9E9E9E;line.bold;text:2a0a4a

  rectangle "**PersistentVolumeClaims**, **Services**,\n**ConfigMaps**, **ServiceAccounts**,\n**NetworkPolicies**\n**get, list, watch, create,**\n**update, patch, delete**\n**Pods**  **get, list, watch, create, delete**\n(a Pod is replaced, never edited)\nNetworkPolicy and ServiceAccount are\nsynthesized per Agent / per AgentTask and\nowner-referenced for cascade GC, so create\nand delete must reach user namespaces.\nlist and watch feed controller-runtime's\ninformers. Pods is cluster-wide also because\nthe AgentReconciler enumerates gateway\nPods in kaalm-system for the activity fan-out." as core #back:F5F5F5;line:9E9E9E;line.bold;text:2a0a4a

  rectangle "**cert-manager.io/v1 Certificate**\n**get, list, watch, create,**\n**update, patch, delete**\nthe per-Agent and per-AgentTask certs live\nalongside the workload, not kaalm-system.\nlist and watch are required so the reconciler\ncan observe status.conditions[type=Ready]\nbefore creating the dependent Pod." as certs #back:F5F5F5;line:9E9E9E;line.bold;text:2a0a4a

  rectangle "**roles**, **rolebindings**\n(rbac.authorization.k8s.io)\n**get, list, watch, create, update, patch, delete**\nno escalate, no bind: every permission the\nminted Roles grant is one the operator\nalready holds cluster-wide" as rbacres #back:F5F5F5;line:9E9E9E;line.bold;text:2a0a4a

  rectangle "**Secrets**\n**get, list, watch**\nin **every** namespace: provider and tool\ncredential validation and probes, and the\nchannel credential key check. Read-only,\nnever copied. The tighter grant the design\npoints at (a kaalm-system read plus escalate\nand bind) is not what the chart grants." as secs #back:FFD580;line:B71C1C;line.bold;text:3a1f00

  rectangle "**Events**  **create, patch**" as meta #back:F5F5F5;line:9E9E9E;line.bold;text:2a0a4a
}

' ---------- family 2: namespaced Role ----------
rectangle "namespace: **kaalm-system**" as nssys #line:0D47A1;line.dashed;text:0a2540 {
  rectangle "**Leases**\n**get, list, watch, create,**\n**update, patch, delete**\ncontroller-runtime's leader-election lock\nneeds the full set. Shipping it as the\nnamespaced Role is what confines it\nto kaalm-system. Events and ConfigMaps\nride the same Role for the lock." as leases #back:FFD580;line:7a3f00;line.bold;text:3a1f00
}

' ---------- family 3: dynamic per-namespace Roles ----------
rectangle "a user namespace, per AgentChannel" as nsuser #line:7a3f00;line.dashed;text:3a1f00 {
  rectangle "channel **Secret(s)**\n**get, watch**\nresourceNames-scoped to the Secret(s) named\nby that AgentChannel's credential config.\n//list omitted//: resourceNames cannot\nconstrain it. A name-scoped watch must set\nfieldSelector metadata.name=<secret>.\n....\nA mirror of the gateway's Role, minted for\nconsistency: the operator's own limit is the\ncluster-wide read above. Torn down with\nthe AgentChannel." as chsec #back:FFD580;line:7a3f00;line.bold;text:3a1f00
}

' ---------- the three edge classes ----------
OPSA -[#B71C1C,bold]-> crds : **ClusterRole**\n+ ClusterRoleBinding
OPSA -[#B71C1C,bold]-> core
OPSA -[#B71C1C,bold]-> certs
OPSA -[#B71C1C,bold]-> rbacres
OPSA -[#B71C1C,bold]-> secs
OPSA -[#B71C1C,bold]-> meta
OPSA -[#0D47A1]-> leases : **Role** + RoleBinding\nin kaalm-system
OPSA .[#7a3f00,bold].> chsec : **dynamic Role**\nper AgentChannel

crds -[hidden]down- core
core -[hidden]down- certs
certs -[hidden]down- rbacres
rbacres -[hidden]down- secs
secs -[hidden]down- meta

legend bottom
  **The same three edge classes as the gateway, and the same ClusterRole/Role split**, for the same reason: a
  ClusterRoleBinding applies in every namespace, so anything that must be namespace-limited (the Lease) ships
  as a separate namespaced Role. The ClusterRole is generated from the reconcilers' RBAC markers and copied into
  the chart, so the figure describes what the chart grants.
  ====
  **The red Secrets box is the one to audit.** The operator's standing Secret read reaches every namespace. It
  writes nothing and copies nothing, but a compromised operator reads every provider key in kaalm-system and every
  channel credential in every user namespace. Escalation prevention is satisfied without escalate or bind because
  the minted per-channel and per-task Roles never grant more than that standing read.
endlegend
@enduml
